nidae) and <italic>Ficus </italic>L</article-title><source>K Ned Akad Wet Verh Afd Natuurk D Tweed Reeks</source><year>1985</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>176</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Compton</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Holton</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Rashbrook</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Noort</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ware</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies of <italic>Ceratosolen galili</italic>, a non-pollinating agaonid fig wasp</article-title><source>Biotropica</source><year>1991</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>188</fpage><lpage>194</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2388305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weiblen</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bush</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Speciation in fig pollinators and parasites</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2002</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>1573</fpage><lpage>1578</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12144676</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-294X.2002.01529.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marussich</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Machado</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Host-specificity and coevolution among pollinating and nonpollinating New World fig wasps</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1925</fpage><lpage>1946</lpage><pub-id p